    "1": {
      "purpose": "Purpose: This Interface Requirements Specification (IRS) defines the interface requirements for the ground segment and sensor interfaces of the defense R&D software project.  The IRS outlines the functionality, data formats, and communication protocols for each interface to ensure seamless integration with the ground segment and sensor systems.\n\nNote: The IRS is based on the design review minutes from Design Review 04 (MoMDesignReview04.docx) and incorporates requirements from the Interface Requirements document (IRSv2.0.docx).",
      "scope": "Scope\n\nThis Interface Requirements Specification (IRS) defines the interface requirements for the ground segment and sensor interfaces of the defense R&D software project.  The IRS outlines the communication protocols, data formats, and functionality required for seamless interaction between the ground segment and sensor interfaces with the software system.\n\nReference: REQ-0001\n\nThis document is based on the design review minutes from Design Review 04 (MoM_DesignReview04.docx) which outlines the preliminary design of the telemetry acquisition subsystem, including decisions regarding sample buffer implementation and REST interface versioning.  Further details can be found in the following documents:\n\nIRS-v2.0.docx: Interface Requirements Specification Revision 2.0\nMoM_DesignReview04.docx: Minutes of Meeting \u2014 Design Review 04\n\nNote: This document will be updated as necessary to reflect changes in requirements and design decisions throughout the project lifecycle.",
