      "encoding": "ICD Section 3: Message Formats and Data Structures - Encoding Rules\n\n3.1 Encoding Rules\n\nThis section outlines the encoding rules for messages exchanged between system components, adhering to the specified protocol defined in api.proto.\n\n3.1.1 Telemetry Sample Envelopes:\n\nInterface IR-0101: The ground segment interface shall transmit telemetry sample envelopes as defined in api.proto (message TelemetrySample).\n    * This message format is based on the TelemetrySample message defined in the api.proto file.\n\n3.1.2 Acquisition Command Interface:\n\nInterface IR-0102: The acquisition command interface shall accept a StartCommand message to begin acquisition.\n    * This message format is based on the StartCommand message defined in the api.proto file.\n\n3.1.3 Health Reporting Interface:\n\nInterface IR-0103: The health reporting interface shall expose an MTBF estimate as defined in api.proto (message HealthReport).\n    * This message format is based on the HealthReport message defined in the api.proto file.\n\n3.1.4 Raw Sample Stream:\n\nInterface IR-04: The sensor interface shall provide a raw sample stream at the configured sample rate.\n    * This requirement is not explicitly defined in the provided text, but it is implied by the need for a raw sample stream to be available for processing.\n\n3.1.5 Encoding and Data Structure:\n\nProtocol: The encoding of messages will adhere to the proto3 syntax as specified in the api.proto file.\n    * This ensures interoperability between different system components.\n\nNote: This ICD section provides a high-level overview of the message formats and data structures used within the project.  Further details on specific encoding rules, data structure definitions, and protocol implementation can be found in the api.proto file and related documentation."
    },
